<resources>
    <!-- Launcher: black field, glassy flame foreground. -->
    <color name="ic_launcher_background">#000000</color>

    <!-- Splash / window base so there is never a white flash before Compose draws. -->
    <color name="window_background_dark">#0A0A0B</color>
    <color name="window_background_light">#FAFAFB</color>

    <!--
      Home-screen widget.

      Its own palette rather than the Compose theme's, for one reason: a
      widget is drawn by the launcher over somebody else's wallpaper, so it
      needs an opaque plate of its own instead of a surface that assumes it
      already has a background. The day values live here and are restated
      whole in values-night — colours do merge across qualifiers, so the
      widget follows the same system dark flag the app does.
    -->
    <color name="widget_surface">#FFFFFFFF</color>
    <color name="widget_ink">#FF131316</color>
    <color name="widget_muted">#FF6A6A73</color>
    <!--
      EmberDim on the white plate rather than Ember. The count sits at 12sp
      bold on a white background, where Ember is 3.58:1 — the accent doing a
      text job it is too light for. EmberDim is the same hue at 5.82:1, and
      the ✓ mark takes it just as well as the number does. values-night
      restates the brighter Ember, where it is the light end of the pair.
    -->
    <color name="widget_accent">#FFB23F06</color>
    <color name="widget_edge">#FFE6E6EA</color>
</resources>
